# Ctrl+P and the PLUGINS tab: the plugin manager (the owner's bug of 2026-10-04: Ctrl+P did
# nothing).
#
# Mission Planner's Ctrl+P is MainV2.ProcessCmdKey's `new PluginUI().Show()` (MainV2.cs:4125-4129),
# and the Drone ID plugin's first-run message tells the user to press it. Here, by the owner's word
# (2026-10-04), the form is the PLUGINS tab, between LOGS and HELP, and Ctrl+P shows that tab. The
# form (Plugin/PluginUI.cs) lists the plugins PluginLoader.Plugins holds - Init and Loaded both
# said yes - green when enabled; Save && Close writes the rows not ticked as DisabledPlugins for
# the next start and shows the restart warning from then on; a disabled plugin is not loaded at
# the next start and is listed dark red, "Not loaded" - here a shipped plugin, built in, counting
# as a file in the plugins folder.
#
# Not the C#'s, the owner's complaint of 2026-10-16 ("we appear to have *two* tailscale plugins,
# and i still have NO IDEA HOW TO USE THEM"): one Tailscale row, and under the grid while it is
# ticked the Tailscale panel - how to use it in three lines, the Guide, this computer's Tailscale
# (tests/gui/fake-tailscale.sh, which the runner gives every script, on a tailnet) and the tick of
# the planner's built-in node, which was a row of its own.
#
# The config holds `tabcontrolactions`, so the Drone ID plugin's message box does not show.
# And an empty `DisabledPlugins`: every plugin on, Open Drone ID too, which is off until a user
# turns it on (the owner, 2026-10-05).
# The built-in plugins: the runner leaves them out unless a script asks for them.
env MP_BUILTIN_PLUGINS 1
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 16
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env MP_OPEN_WITH_SHELL_LOG $WORK/opened.txt
setup printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config><tabcontrolactions>tabQuick;</tabcontrolactions><DisabledPlugins></DisabledPlugins></Config>' > "$WORK/config.xml"
expect plugins.Dowding.state running
expect plugins.question none
expect plugin-manager.open false
# The key, on the flight screen with nothing focused: the PLUGINS tab.
key ctrl+p
expect screen plugins
expect plugin-manager.open true
expect plugin-manager.restart-required false
# The seven running plugins, by file name; the three whose Init said no are not in Plugins. Last,
# the owner's native rows (2026-10-14), like a plugin's: Tailscale and Import from Mission Planner,
# on until unticked. The built-in node is no row.
expect plugin-manager.rows 9
expect plugin-manager.row.0 ~ |anonymizebinlog.wasm|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.row.1 Dowding|dowding.wasm|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.row.6 ~ |terrainmaker.wasm|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.row.7 Tailscale|tailscale.native|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.row.8 Import from Mission Planner|mpimport.native|enabled|green
# The Tailscale panel under the grid: its three lines, this computer's Tailscale in the words the
# connection area's indicator uses, and the node's tick, unticked - off until it is ticked whatever
# DisabledPlugins says - with no node and nothing under it.
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.panel true
expect plugin-manager-tailscale below plugin-manager-enabled-tailscale.native
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.step.1 1. Install Tailscale on this computer and on the vehicle's computer, and sign both into your tailnet (or tick the built-in node below and open its sign-in link).
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.step.2 2. In the port box choose Tailscale.
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.step.3 3. CONNECT and type the vehicle's tailnet name or 100.x address.
within 12
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.computer Tailscale: on tailnet as buzz-laptop, 100.101.102.103
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.tick false
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.line none
expect tailnet-node.state stopped
# The Guide hands using_tailscale.md to the desktop's browser, as HELP's Using Tailscale does.
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.opened none
click plugin-manager-tailscale-guide
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.opened https://github.com/davidbuzz/MissionPlannerRust/blob/main/using_tailscale.md
# Tailscale's row unticked, its panel goes at once, before any Save; ticked again, it is back.
click plugin-manager-enabled-tailscale.native
expect plugin-manager.row.7 Tailscale|tailscale.native|disabled|green
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.panel false
click plugin-manager-enabled-tailscale.native
expect plugin-manager.row.7 Tailscale|tailscale.native|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.tailscale.panel true
# Show Errors: every plugin loaded or refused by its own Init, so none.
click plugin-manager-errors
expect plugin-manager.errors No Errors
click plugin-manager-errors-ok
expect plugin-manager.errors none
# Dowding unticked, saved: the tab fills again, Dowding still loaded and now on the disabled list -
# dark orange - and the restart warning shown.
click plugin-manager-enabled-1
expect plugin-manager.row.1 Dowding|dowding.wasm|disabled|green
click plugin-manager-save
expect plugin-manager.restart-required true
expect plugin-manager.row.1 Dowding|dowding.wasm|disabled|dark-orange
# Leaving the tab puts the form away; the tab itself shows it again.
click tab-fly
expect plugin-manager.open false
click tab-plugins
expect plugin-manager.open true
expect plugin-manager.row.1 Dowding|dowding.wasm|disabled|dark-orange
# The node's tick: ticked, Save & Close is what starts it; saved, EnabledNativePlugins names it,
# the node starts at once, and the tab fills again with the tick ticked and the node's state under
# it. The runner's planner is built without the node (mp-gui's `tailnet-node` feature off, as in
# every release), so it fails at once - "this build has no built-in Tailscale node" - and reaches
# nothing; a build with the node would reach Tailscale's servers from this test.
click plugin-manager-tailnet-node-tick
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.tick true
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.line stopped (Save & Close starts it)
click plugin-manager-save
expect plugins.enabled-native tailscale-node.native
expect plugins.disabled dowding.wasm
expect tailnet-node.state failed
expect tailnet-node.said failed: this build has no built-in Tailscale node
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.tick true
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.line failed: this build has no built-in Tailscale node
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.sign-in none
# The next start loads Dowding no more, and lists it "Not loaded", dark red, after the running six;
# the node's tick is kept, and the node started with the planner.
restart
expect plugins.count 9
expect plugins.FenceDist.state running
expect tailnet-node.state failed
key ctrl+p
expect screen plugins
expect plugin-manager.rows 9
expect plugin-manager.row.6 Not loaded|dowding.wasm|disabled|dark-red
expect plugin-manager.row.7 Tailscale|tailscale.native|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.row.8 Import from Mission Planner|mpimport.native|enabled|green
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.tick true
# Dowding ticked again and the node unticked, saved: the node stopped at once and its key back in
# DisabledPlugins; Dowding enabled for the start after. (A moment first: the restarted planner's
# controls are written after its facts.)
settle 1
click plugin-manager-tailnet-node-tick
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.tick false
expect plugin-manager.tailnet-node.line none
click plugin-manager-enabled-6
click plugin-manager-save
expect tailnet-node.state stopped
expect plugins.enabled-native none
expect plugins.disabled tailscale-node.native
restart
expect plugins.Dowding.state running
expect plugins.count 10
expect tailnet-node.state stopped
